\\frac{∂h}{∂\\theta } & =\\frac{∂h}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂h}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta }+\\frac{∂h}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂\\theta } \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂h}{∂x}r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{∂h}{∂y}r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $h$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x}=yz,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂y}=xz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r,\\theta ,$ and $z,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =rz\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta , \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =rz\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂\\theta } & =-(rz\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +(rz\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-{r}^{2}z{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}z{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={r}^{2}z({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={r}^{2}z\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480735 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480735 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480735 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480735 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480735 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480735 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480735 #edb/ref 1045 "Moments of Inertia of Laminas About the Coordinate Axes" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480735 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186481447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480735 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480735 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480735 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "b9cbbc27-45ef-5880-94d7-dce54c0b25ad" #e